    "content": "                                Structural basis of liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism of CNS-targeted AAV capsids | CaltechAUTHORS          [Skip to main](#main)\n\n[![CaltechAUTHORS](/static/images/CaltechAUTHORS-by-Caltech-Library-blue-with-padding.svg)](/)\n\n[Communities](/communities)\n\n[My dashboard](/me/uploads)\n\n[Log in](/login/?next=/records/2qscm-gs990)\n\n![](https://authors.library.caltech.edu/api/communities/aedd135f-227e-4fdf-9476-5b3fd011bac6/logo)\n\n[CaltechAUTHORS](/communities/caltechauthors/records)\n\nPublished July 1, 2026 | Version Published\n\nJournal Article Open\n\n# Structural basis of liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism of CNS-targeted AAV capsids\n\n### Creators\n\n-   [Brittain, Tyler J.1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Brittain,+Tyler+J.%22)\n-   [Jang, Seongmin1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Jang,+Seongmin%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9822-6790 \"Jang, Seongmin's ORCID profile\")\n-   [Coughlin, Gerard M.1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Coughlin,+Gerard+M.%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0644-4721 \"Coughlin, Gerard M.'s ORCID profile\")\n-   [Hoang, Jonathan D.1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Hoang,+Jonathan+D.%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3762-9596 \"Hoang, Jonathan D.'s ORCID profile\")\n-   [Barcelona, Bre'Anna H.1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Barcelona,+Bre'Anna+H.%22)\n-   [Giriat, Izabela1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Giriat,+Izabela%22)\n-   [Ristic, Fiona1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Ristic,+Fiona%22)\n-   [Appling, Nathan1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Appling,+Nathan%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9488-6621 \"Appling, Nathan's ORCID profile\")\n-   [Chossis, Camille PMA1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Chossis,+Camille+PMA%22)\n-   [Shay, Timothy F.1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Shay,+Timothy+F.%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6591-3271 \"Shay, Timothy F.'s ORCID profile\")\n-   [Gradinaru, Viviana1](/search?q=metadata.creators.person_or_org.name:%22Gradinaru,+Viviana%22) [![ORCID icon](/static/images/orcid.svg)](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5868-348X \"Gradinaru, Viviana's ORCID profile\")\n\nShow affiliations\n\n-   1\\. [![ROR icon](/static/images/ror-icon.svg) ](https://ror.org/05dxps055 \"California Institute of Technology's ROR profile\")California Institute of Technology\n\n## Abstract\n\nDeveloping effective vectors for gene therapy requires accurate on-target coverage while minimizing off-target transduction that can lead to adverse events. In mice, the engineered capsid PHP.eB shows enhanced brain transduction, while the further engineered CAP-B10 is also de-targeted from astrocytes and liver. Here, we solved cryoelectron microscopy (cryo-EM) structures of CAP-B10 and its complex with the adeno-associated virus receptor (AAVR) domain PKD2, at 2.22- and 2.20-Å resolutions, respectively. These structures reveal a motif that hinders AAVR binding, which we confirmed by measuring affinities. We showed that this motif is transferable to other capsids by solving cryo-EM structures of AAV9-X1, at 3.09 Å, and AAV9-X1.1 without and with PKD2, at 2.51 and 2.18 Å, respectively. Using this structural information, we designed and validated novel AAV variants with reduced liver and altered brain cell tropism *in vivo*. Overall, we provide a framework for using structural information to guide rational engineering of gene delivery vectors to achieve safe and effective delivery.\n\n## Copyright and License\n\n© 2026 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Inc. on behalf of The American Society of Gene and Cell Therapy. This is an open access article under the CC BY license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).\n\n## Acknowledgement\n\nWe thank all Gradinaru lab and CLOVER staff members for their thoughtful assistance. We thank Alex Jin Chung and Yaping Lei for technical support. We thank Catherine Oikonomou for help with manuscript editing. All cryo-EM data were collected at the Caltech cryo-EM facility. Biolayer interferometry data were collected in the Caltech Protein Expression Center (PEC). We are especially thankful to Songye Chen (Caltech cryo-EM facility director) and Jost Vielmetter (Caltech PEC director) for supporting our data collection. We thank Travis Bainbridge and Beyza Bulutoglu for helpful discussions about optimizing BLI for AAVs. This project was supported by the Beckman Institute CLOVER Center (to T.F.S. and V.G.), NIH PIONEER [DP1NS111369](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1525001626002157?via%3Dihub#gs3) (to V.G.), and NIH BRAIN Initiative Armamentarium [UF1MH128336](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1525001626002157?via%3Dihub#gs4) (to V.G. and T.F.S.). V.G. is an Investigator of the Howard Hughes Medical Institute. Schematic in the manuscript was created with [BioRender.com](https://www.biorender.com/).\n\n## Contributions\n\nTyler J. Brittain and Seongmin Jang contributed equally.\n\nS.J. and V.G. conceived and T.J.B., S.J., T.F.S., and V.G. designed the study. T.J.B. performed cryo-EM data collection and processing. T.B. and S.J. analyzed the structure data. S.J. performed and analyzed the BLI experiments. T.J.B., S.J., and N.A. performed molecular cloning. S.J. performed the receptor protein production. C.P.M.A.C. performed the size-exclusion chromatography. S.J. performed the pull-down assays. I.G. performed the cell infectivity assays. G.M.C., J.D.H., B.H.B., and F.R. performed the mouse injections, perfusions, and tissue staining. G.M.C. and S.J. performed the Keyence imaging. T.J.B. and J.D.H. performed the confocal imaging. T.J.B. quantified liver de-targeting and brain tropism. S.J. quantified muscle transduction. G.M.C. and S.J. performed ddPCR. T.J.B. and S.J. wrote the manuscript and prepared the figures. V.G. supervised all aspects of the work.\n\n## Data Availability\n\nCryo-EM maps and atomic models have been deposited with the accession codes EMDB (Electron Microscopy Data Bank): 71273 and PDB: [9P4L](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4L) (CAP-B10), EMDB: 71278 and PDB: [9P4Q](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4Q) (CAP-B10-PKD2), EMDB: 71277 and PDB: [9P4P](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4P) (AAV9-X1), EMDB: 71279 and PDB: [9P4R](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4R) (AAV9-X1.1), EMDB: 71275 and PDB: [9P4N](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4N) (AAV9-X1.1-PKD2), EMDB: 71274 and PDB: [9P4M](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4M) (AAV9-B10), and EMDB: 71276 and PDB: [9P4O](http://www.rcsb.org/pdb/explore.do?structureId=9P4O) (eB.24).\n\n## Conflict of Interest\n\nV.G. is a cofounder of Capsida Biotherapeutics, a fully integrated AAV engineering and gene therapy company.\n\n## Files\n\n### \n\n1-s2.0-S1525001626002157-mmc2.pdf\n\n### \n\nFiles (35.7 MB)\n\nName\n\nSize\n\n[1-s2.0-S1525001626002157-mmc2.pdf](/records/2qscm-gs990/files/1-s2.0-S1525001626002157-mmc2.pdf?download=1)\n\nmd5:e4e6899da159dc0ce7b21ef749f18707\n\n35.7 MB\n\n[Preview](/records/2qscm-gs990/preview/1-s2.0-S1525001626002157-mmc2.pdf?include_deleted=0) [Download](/records/2qscm-gs990/files/1-s2.0-S1525001626002157-mmc2.pdf?download=1)\n\n## Additional details\n\n### Identifiers\n\nPMID\n\n[41906393](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41906393/ \"Opens in new tab\")\n\n### Funding\n\nHoward Hughes Medical Institute\n\nNational Institutes of Health\n\nDP1NS111369\n\nNational Institutes of Health\n\nUF1MH128336\n\n### \n\nCaltech Custom Metadata\n\nCaltech groups[](https://library.caltech.edu/groups)\n\n[Division of Biology and Biological En