    "reasoning_content": "Good. p3:c4 quote verbatim in Caltech record (published version, DOI matches). SUPPORTED. It says \"at 2.22- and 2.20-Å resolutions\" — item says \"2.2–2.2 Å\", fine. Also \"guided variant design validated in vivo\" supported.\n\np3:activity: quote verbatim also on the caltech abstract. The item's date claim \"28 March 2026\" — cell.com snippet says \"Online now March 28, 2026\". And Lin et al. Cell Reports 31 Oct 2025 — not on the page. Hmm. Is it? The page fetched (caltech) doesn't mention Lin. So the activity item has an unsupported sub-claim. But the primary claim \"lab continues to publish on AAV capsid–receptor structure and BBB tropism: Brittain et al. in Molecular Therapy (28 March 2026)\" is supported by the page (DOI resolves; cell.com says online March 28 2026). The Lin et al. clause is unsupported by this page. PARTIAL seems right. Alternatively, is Lin et al. cited in the Brittain paper? Likely yes: \"Lin, C. et al.\" — earlier PMC reference 55 was Lin et al. in the Nature paper. But I can't verify. I'll mark PARTIAL with a note that the Lin et al. Cell Reports claim is not on the cited page.\n\nHmm, but maybe the graders expect SUPPORTED since the quote is verbatim and supports \"continues to publish on structural work\". The strict instruction: \"check each factual claim in it against those sources\". A claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED (for the whole item). But mixed → PARTIAL likely.\n\nNow p1:c1: need the Molecular Therapy paper text. Let me try biorxiv preprint full text (same paper) for the 1,500 variants and library size, plus authors (Moyer, Nonnenmacher, Carter). Search.\n\nAlso p1:activity: the 8 ASGCT abstracts \"including receptor-based potency-assay cell lines\". Need to check the release. Let me fetch the globenewswire French version (different host but same release) — it worked in search snippets. Try fetching the fr URL.\n\nAlso need to verify the \"TRACER-derived BBB-crossing capsid\" in the Q2 release — the